WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.658 --> 00:00:17.560
Morb was still in the dungeon, waiting for the trolls to arrive with the leeches.

2
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:25.044
"So, Morb," Boz taunted, clutching the bars of his cell, "what happened to your prisoners at the zoo?

3
00:00:25.905 --> 00:00:28.466
My friend Teplo told me they all escaped.

4
00:00:28.947 --> 00:00:31.188
Now how could that have happened?"

5
00:00:31.904 --> 00:00:34.006
In the next cell, Teplo smirked.

6
00:00:34.406 --> 00:00:36.048
"Well, Boz, let me tell you.

7
00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:40.771
Apparently Morb's trolls were tricked by a pile of turnips."

8
00:00:42.693 --> 00:00:44.094
"Turnips, you say?"

9
00:00:44.414 --> 00:00:45.095
Boz laughed.

10
00:00:45.855 --> 00:00:48.177
"That is correct," said Teplo.

11
00:00:48.858 --> 00:00:52.461
"Perhaps Morb's not as powerful as he thinks he is, huh?"

12
00:00:53.302 --> 00:00:58.185
Morb ignored the old men, his gaze moving past them to a couple huddled together in a cell

13
00:00:58.286 --> 00:00:59.386
farther down the corridor.

14
00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:00.908
He walked toward them.

15
00:01:03.148 --> 00:01:07.289
"Hello, Mother and Father," he greeted them with a twisted smile.

16
00:01:07.309 --> 00:01:10.610
"I hope the accommodations suit you."

17
00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.411
His mother looked up with tears in her eyes.

18
00:01:13.431 --> 00:01:16.332
"Why are you doing this, Morb?"

19
00:01:16.532 --> 00:01:17.052
she whispered.

20
00:01:17.072 --> 00:01:19.272
"Don't let him get to you, Mother!"

21
00:01:19.653 --> 00:01:22.013
a handsome young Red called from a few cells down.

22
00:01:22.033 --> 00:01:24.554
"He never did appreciate you."

23
00:01:24.574 --> 00:01:31.636
"True, I didn't appreciate being ignored and misunderstood," Morb snapped, glaring at his brother.

24
00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:34.385
Meanwhile his father climbed to his feet.

25
00:01:34.405 --> 00:01:38.587
"Son, please think about what you're doing," he said.

26
00:01:38.607 --> 00:01:41.809
"Didn't we teach you right from wrong?"

27
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.690
Morb turned away from him.

28
00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:48.933
"You taught me that I'd better do whatever was necessary to take care of myself.

29
00:01:49.773 --> 00:01:51.374
And I learned that lesson well."

30
00:01:52.755 --> 00:01:54.916
"Nobody had to teach you to be selfish, Morb!"

31
00:01:55.236 --> 00:01:57.918
a young woman—one of his sisters—called from nearby.

32
00:01:57.938 --> 00:01:59.999
"You were born that way!"

33
00:02:00.699 --> 00:02:01.800
Morb ignored her too.

34
00:02:02.164 --> 00:02:04.705
He'd just heard heavy footsteps coming down the stairs.

35
00:02:05.465 --> 00:02:06.965
Good. The trolls were here.

36
00:02:06.985 --> 00:02:12.907
"Bring the cauldron to me," he called to them, not looking at his parents as his mother started

37
00:02:12.947 --> 00:02:13.487
to sob.

38
00:02:13.507 --> 00:02:17.148
"We'll start right here, in this cell."

39
00:02:17.168 --> 00:02:23.290
"I wish I had a map," Zann muttered, peeking around a corner.

40
00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:25.871
"I've got to get back to my friends."

41
00:02:26.671 --> 00:02:30.812
Zann had been walking through the palace for some time and had not yet found an exit.

42
00:02:31.524 --> 00:02:35.348
All he'd found were winding stairways and dark, narrow corridors.

43
00:02:36.169 --> 00:02:38.351
The palace was much bigger than he'd realized.

44
00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:44.416
Creeping down another flight of steps, Zann diligently watched for any trolls that might be around.

45
00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:47.339
He thought briefly about just zapping out.

46
00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.643
After all, that Deceleration spell hadn't attracted Morb's attention.

47
00:02:52.063 --> 00:02:53.785
But it probably wasn't worth the risk.

48
00:02:53.925 --> 00:02:55.487
There had to be a way out somewhere.

49
00:02:55.507 --> 00:03:01.445
"Aha!" Zann whispered when he saw sunlight pouring in through a large doorway at the end of a

50
00:03:01.505 --> 00:03:02.246
long hallway.

51
00:03:03.326 --> 00:03:04.126
He hurried forward.

52
00:03:04.846 --> 00:03:09.868
But the doorway was not an exit—it led to a balcony overlooking the huge courtyard at the center

53
00:03:09.908 --> 00:03:10.468
of the palace.

54
00:03:10.488 --> 00:03:12.649
"What in the world is that?"

55
00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:18.091
Zann blurted out in surprise when he saw the huge, dark, hulking shape in the middle of the

56
00:03:18.151 --> 00:03:22.292
courtyard. Zann immediately thought about what Gliss had told them yesterday.

57
00:03:23.072 --> 00:03:28.175
Could this be the horrible magic-sucking machine that Morb had built to help him take over Magica?

58
00:03:29.716 --> 00:03:32.457
He was still staring at the machine when he heard voices approaching.

59
00:03:32.857 --> 00:03:33.978
One of them belonged to Slib.

60
00:03:33.998 --> 00:03:36.219
"Uh-oh," Zann whispered.

61
00:03:36.439 --> 00:03:38.020
There was nowhere to hide on the balcony.

62
00:03:38.721 --> 00:03:41.422
Looking around, Zann saw some pebbles in a planter.

63
00:03:41.662 --> 00:03:42.683
They gave him an idea.

64
00:03:43.383 --> 00:03:47.345
He picked up one of the pebbles and threw it down the hall, past Slib and the others.

65
00:03:48.106 --> 00:03:49.486
It hit a wall and made a sound.

66
00:03:50.027 --> 00:03:52.068
Click! "What was that?"

67
00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:53.104
said Slib.

68
00:03:53.764 --> 00:03:57.465
Everyone turned around, and Zann quickly dashed into a room across the hall.

69
00:03:57.485 --> 00:04:03.427
"I'm sure it's nothing," said someone else, as the group continued walking closer to Zann.

70
00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:08.288
Zann held his breath—he could hear Slib and the others right outside the door.

71
00:04:08.308 --> 00:04:16.251
"You can believe what I say since I'm now Morb's most trusted adviser," Slib was bragging.

72
00:04:16.271 --> 00:04:21.012
"The era of Reds is truly over, just as I predicted.

73
00:04:21.804 --> 00:04:27.188
Thanks to King Morb, the rest of us will now have the power we deserve."

74
00:04:28.128 --> 00:04:31.631
One of his companions murmured something in response, but Zann wasn't listening.

75
00:04:32.331 --> 00:04:36.954
He barely had time to dash through another doorway before Slib and the others came into the room.

76
00:04:37.995 --> 00:04:41.177
Zann found himself in a hallway lined with half a dozen doors.

77
00:04:42.138 --> 00:04:45.160
Behind him, he could hear Slib still bragging loudly.

78
00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.341
Zann reached for the first door.

79
00:04:47.361 --> 00:04:51.124
"Ouch!" he blurted out, as the doorknob burned his hand.

80
00:04:51.892 --> 00:04:52.693
"Did you hear that?"

81
00:04:53.173 --> 00:04:55.214
Slib's muffled voice came from the other room.

82
00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:58.196
"There's someone behind that door."

83
00:04:59.297 --> 00:04:59.958
Zann gulped.

84
00:05:00.238 --> 00:05:01.218
He had to get out of sight!

85
00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:06.422
But when he looked down the hall, all the doorknobs were glowing red, just like the one he'd

86
00:05:06.482 --> 00:05:09.324
touched. No—not all of them.

87
00:05:10.045 --> 00:05:12.386
He spotted one doorknob that was glowing blue.

88
00:05:13.127 --> 00:05:15.328
He hurried toward it, but then he hesitated.

89
00:05:15.688 --> 00:05:18.130
Who had put a spell on these doors, and why?

90
00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.672
He'd never seen this kind of spell before.

91
00:05:21.416 --> 00:05:25.719
Normally people just used an ordinary Shield spell if they wanted to keep others out of a room.

92
00:05:26.739 --> 00:05:29.241
Then he heard the door behind him start to open.

93
00:05:29.881 --> 00:05:32.723
If he didn't get out of this hallway, Slib would see him!

94
00:05:33.363 --> 00:05:37.125
Grabbing the blue doorknob, he was relieved to find it cool under his hand.

95
00:05:37.845 --> 00:05:41.047
He pushed through the door, allowing it to fall shut behind him.

96
00:05:41.688 --> 00:05:45.690
He found himself in what appeared to be a dusty old storage room.

97
00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:49.032
The only light came through a single barred window.

98
00:05:49.728 --> 00:05:54.996
Boxes and crates were piled everywhere, and a couple of dust bugs scuttled off behind a trunk.

99
00:05:55.777 --> 00:05:57.219
Zann heard a sound behind him.

100
00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.662
Spinning around, he gasped.

101
00:06:00.483 --> 00:06:05.470
Standing in a dim corner of the room was the old woman he and his friends had met

102
00:06:05.591 --> 00:06:06.312
in Wormwood.
